    <!-- First-start terms for Brief You (Read You's own text names Read You and its repo). -->
    <string name="brief_tos_tips">Please read and agree to Brief You\'s terms of service and privacy policy to continue.</string>
    <string name="brief_tos_content"><h5> Privacy policy </h5> <br /> <p> <b>Brief You</b> does not collect any user data. Your feeds, articles and settings, and any account passwords, stay in the app\'s storage on your device. AI summaries run on your device with a model you add yourself; nothing is sent anywhere for them. </p> <br /> <p> <b>Brief You</b> uses these permissions: </p> <br /> <p> - Network access (to fetch the feeds and pages you choose) </p> <p> - Network status (to know whether you are online, or on Wi-Fi) </p> <p> - Background work and notifications (to sync on a schedule, and for read aloud) </p> <br /> <br /> <h5> Third-party services </h5> <br /> <p> This policy does not cover services you use with <b>Brief You</b>, such as an RSS server. See their own privacy policies. </p> <br /> <br /> <h5> Disclaimers </h5> <br /> <p> <b>Brief You</b> is only a tool for reading content you choose. You are responsible for using it within the laws of your country or region. </p> <br /> <br /> <h5> Open source license </h5> <br /> <p> <b>Brief You</b> is a fork of Read You[1], and like it is open source under the GNU GPL 3.0 license[2]: you may use, study and change the source code for free, but changed or derived versions may not be distributed as closed-source software. </p> <br /> <br /> <h5> Appendix </h5> <br /> <p> - [1] https://github.com/Humorist2601/BriefYou (based on https://github.com/ReadYouApp/ReadYou) </p> <p> - [2] https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html </p></string>
